# The same program again, over a file it cannot read: an export whose columns
# are named something else entirely. This is the guard in
# examples/statement.vine firing -- a guard nobody has watched fire does not
# work -- and until tick 41 it was also the reason the whole report was
# wrapped in a function, because `return` is legal nowhere else.
#
# Note the exit status, and where the three lines are. They go to stderr and
# the status is 1, so `vine statement.vine < this && publish` does not
# publish, and a pipe on the other end of it gets nothing rather than prose
# where a report should be. Both were the other way about in tick 40; see
# **Refusing** in docs/spec.md.
examples/statement.vine
